SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] MaineCare Notice of Agency Rule-making Propos
 al\, MaineCare Benefits Manual\, Chapter III\, Section 20\, Allowances for
  Home and Community-Based Services for Adults with Other Related Condition
 s
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			MaineCare Notice of Agency Rule-making Proposal\, Maine
 Care Benefits Manual\, Chapter III\, Section 20\, Allowances for Home and 
 Community-Based Services for Adults with Other Related Conditions\nMaineCa
 re Notice of Agency Rule-making Proposal\, MaineCare Benefits Manual\, Cha
 pter III\, Section 20\, Allowances for Home and Community-Based Services f
 or Adults with Other Related Conditions\nAug 26\, 2026\nThe Division of Po
 licy posts all proposed and recently adopted rules on\nMaineCare’s Polic
 y and Rules webpage\n. This website keeps the rules on file until they are
  finalized and until the Secretary of State website is updated to reflect 
 the changes. The MaineCare Benefits Manual is available on-line at the\nSe
 cretary of State’s website\n.\nBelow\, please find a MaineCare Notice of
  Agency Rulemaking Proposal. You can access the complete rule at\nhttp://w
 ww.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/rules/index.shtml.\n________________________________
 ____________________________________________\nNotice of Agency Rulemaking 
 Proposal\nAGENCY:\nDepartment of Health and Human Services\, Office of Mai
 neCare Services\, Division of Policy\nCHAPTER NUMBER AND RULE TITLE:\n10-1
 44 C.M.R. Ch. 101\, MaineCare Benefits Manual (MBM)\, Ch. III\, Sec. 20\, 
 Allowances for Home and Community-Based Services for Adults with Other Rel
 ated Conditions\nTYPE OF RULE:\nMajor Substantive\nBRIEF SUMMARY:\nSection
  20 in the MBM authorizes home and community-based services (HCBS) under a
  CMS-approved Section 1915(c) waiver. The Department proposes to amend the
  Chapter III\, Section 20 rule to establish the reimbursement methodology 
 for new services being added under a companion\, Chapter II\, Section 20 r
 ule\, and to remove rates of reimbursement for all services which will now
  be listed in Rate Schedules on the Department’s website pursuant to 22 
 M.R.S. § 3177-J. The website address for current rates of reimbursement i
 n the D\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/maine
 care-notice-agency-rule-making-proposal-mainecare-benefits-manual-chapter-
 iii-3
